# The manifest (web/rounds.json) is tracked and the media (web/clips/) is not.
#
# The manifest has to be: functions/api/score.js imports it at build time, so the
# five rounds the server checks a daily play against are by construction the five
# the page handed out. It is a few KB and carries no coordinates.
#
# The media cannot be. A round set is ~125 MB of mp4 and this repo is public, so
# committing one would add that to history on every regeneration, permanently and
# irreversibly. It goes to R2 instead (`task clips:push`), which CI pulls before
# deploying. The trade is that a deploy is not self-contained: the manifest and
# the media can disagree, and smoke.sh is what catches it.
#
# A generation in progress is neither: make_rounds.py builds into .staging and
# moves the previous clips aside, and no part of that belongs in a deploy.
web/clips/
web/.staging/
web/clips.old/

# The answers. make_rounds.py writes these next to the round set rather than
# inside web/, because web/ is the entire deployed surface — a coords file in
# there would just be fetchable. They reach production through D1
# (`task answers:{stage,prod}:push`), never through git: this is a public repo,
# and a committed answer key is the same leak as a manifest full of coordinates.
answers.json
answers.sql

# Stamped into the deploy by staging.yml / release.yml — which build this is,
# and the changelog to go with it. Generated per deploy, never committed.
web/version.json

# `task dev`'s local D1 and wrangler's scratch state.
.wrangler/

__pycache__/
.venv/
.DS_Store
.ruff_cache/
